ep_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Under the required 600-unit inter-event gap, 695 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1495 (step_01). This is not an artefact of missing activity: both endpoints are active in the window with several distinct partners (step_03). Relaxing the waiting limit altogether still fails \u2014 695 temporally reaches 588 nodes but not 1495 (step_04) \u2014 so no time-respecting sequence of any pacing connects them. The large static 3-hop neighbourhood around 695 (step_02) shows why an order-ignoring view could misleadingly suggest connectivity; volume and static proximity are the confounders here, and the temporal ordering rules the cascade out."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no cascade.**\n\n- **step_01**: With the 600-unit relay constraint, only 2 nodes are temporally reachable from 695 in the window \u2014 1495 is not among them.\n- **step_03**: Both nodes are active (695: 5 events/5 partners; 1495: 4 events/4 partners), so the negative result is not due to an inactive/absent endpoint.\n- **step_04**: Even relaxing the constraint entirely (unbounded waiting), 695 temporally reaches 588 nodes but still never 1495 \u2014 the failure is directional/temporal, not a matter of gap tolerance.\n- **step_02**: 695 sits in a large, densely connected 3-hop static neighbourhood, confirming that any apparent \"connection\" when time is ignored is a confounder rather than evidence of influence flow.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [695, 1495],\n  \"window\": [28025, 66424],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the required 600-unit inter-event gap, 695 reaches only 2 nodes and never 1495 (step_01). This is not an artefact of missing activity: both endpoints are active in the window with several distinct partners (step_03). Relaxing the waiting limit altogether still fails \u2014 695 temporally reaches 588 nodes but not 1495 (step_04) \u2014 so no time-respecting sequence of any pacing connects them. The large static 3-hop neighbourhood around 695 (step_02) shows why an order-ignoring view could misleadingly suggest connectivity; volume and static proximity are the confounders here, and the temporal ordering rules the cascade out.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 17692, "total_output_tokens": 1345, "total_tokens": 19037, "total_latency_ms": 22492, "llm_calls": 3, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}